 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Email is polite but vague. A quick phone call says it's serious without embarrassing them. Which do you prefer? Then tell her directly, in an email or during a chat. Ask her to keep it to herself though, so the surprise is intact. Then listen to her and include her as a plus one. Weddings are shared gifts, and she's still part of the team if only as a friend. classic toast after the cake is the proper spot. Go for it. Good plan. And if she does come, be the big sharer of the sweet spot.",
